 "answer": "To get the on-disk size of a pgvector index in Postgres, you can use the `pg_size_pretty` function in combination with `pg_relation_size`. According to the context provided, the query you would use is:\n\n```sql\nSELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size('index_name'));\n```\n\nReplace `'index_name'` with the actual name of your pgvector index to retrieve its size in a human-readable format. This method is applicable to any index in Postgres, including pgvector indexes.",
